-- title:
--   Branches above the j-line for Γ₁(M)∩Γ₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 5$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a characteristic-zero field that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p \in \mathfrak{m}_A$, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating $\mathfrak{m}_A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of the $j$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNum}$, and let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ for some $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ sending $j$ to the series $j(q^p)$, such that the pullback $\sigma^{-1}W_0$ differs from $W_0$ yet contains $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every $P \in A[X]$ with nonzero reduction. Four assertions follow. (i) Any valuation subring $V$ of $K$ containing the image of $A$, with the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ inside the nonunits of $V$, and containing $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for all $P \in A[X]$ of nonzero reduction, equals $W_0$ or $\sigma^{-1}W_0$. (ii) For any such $V$, every $f$ in the nonunits of $V$ is $\varpi g$ with $g \in V$. (iii) Any intermediate field $R_0$ of $\kappa(A) \subseteq \kappa(A)((q))$ whose elements are exactly the ratios $\bar{x}/\bar{y}$ arising from such presentations $f \cdot y = x$ with $f \in K$, $x,y \in A[[q]]$, $\bar{y} \neq 0$, equals the field generated over $\kappa(A)$ by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(M)$. (iv) The relative degree of $K$ over the $L$-base change of the level-$M$ field $X_1(M)$ equals $p+1$.
--
--   This is the local description, at a place above $p$, of the two branches of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$ over the generic point of the $j$-line: two valuation rings, each with $\varpi$ as uniformiser, the Gauss reductions of one of them being exactly the level-$M$ function field in characteristic $p$, and the total relative degree $p+1$. It feeds the subsequent results on ramification, residue fields and separability for these branches.
